title: $:/plugins/nikorion/pkm-schema/fields/maturity
tags: $:/tags/nikorion/pkm/Field
kind: vocab
list: stub rough stable
blank-value: stub
applies-filter: [<currentTiddler>!role[log]!role[decision]!role[task]!role[tasklist]]
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

One value from the vocabulary in `list`, in display order.

`stub` is the blank value (`blank-value`): it stands for the empty field and is never stored — choosing it clears the field. A tiddler with no maturity is a stub: list the stubs with `[!has[maturity]]`, not `[maturity[stub]]`.

`applies-filter` says where the field means something: registers (`log`, `decision`) are dated and only ever added to, and tasks have their own `status`. Written `!role[…]` rather than `get[role]!match[…]`, which would return nothing on a tiddler with no role.
